    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nHello!\n\nI'm on Colemak (yikes) so I have really weird bindings. I want to use `i` as the prefix for `inside` commands in `operator-pending` mode, but use `h` in `visual` mode because I use `i` to move right.\n\nWould it be possible to have something like:\n\n```lua\nmappings = {\n    o = {\n        inside = \"i\",\n        inside_next = \"in\",\n        inside_last = \"il\",\n    },\n\n    v = {\n        inside = \"h\",\n        inside_next = \"hn\",\n        inside_last = \"hl\",\n    },\n},\n```\n\nbut still allow the current keymap format to apply to both modes by default?\n\nThis is a really niche use-case (like it might just be me) so if there is another work-around I'm happy to go for that instead.\n\nThank you!",
    "closed_at": "2026-06-15T11:54:24Z",
